out.push(h2('16.7  Review & Mediate: The assessor and the assessed'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 16 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _The returns **count** for half…_   **2** _A criterion **which** cannot be failed…_   **3** _…assessed **against** three criteria…_   **4** _The verdict is **appealable** within ten days._   **5** _His **objectivity** in the marking…_   **6** _The panel **moderated** the marks…_'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **The page is missing what the failed criterion _means_** — **whether it is a note for next year, a condition on the verdict, or a record somebody else will read in two years.** **The one sentence that would supply it:** _the failed criterion is a note for your second year; it is not a condition and it does not go beyond this file_ — **or the opposite, if the opposite is true.** **And if the assessor does not know, that is the answer and it is still given:** _I do not know whether anybody else reads this file and I shall find out and tell you by Thursday._'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This cycle is the only one in the unit where the page is not at fault, and the whole lesson depends on the class accepting that.** **Mrs Nasser\'s page does everything 16.1 to 16.6 teach** — **failable criteria, a published weighting, working with its sources, a verdict fourth, an appeal route with a date, and her own weakest line named** — **and the candidate still cannot read it.** **Both accounts are accurate.** ⚠ **So the standing warning takes its Unit 16 form: do not improve the page.** **The room will want to redraft it, because redrafting is what the unit has trained them to do, and it answers nothing.** **The gap is not in the drafting.** ⚠ **And the finding to send them away with is the one that is new to the book:** **a page can satisfy every criterion in this unit and still leave the person unable to act, because the five parts say how the verdict was reached and not what to do about it.** **One line closes it, and nobody writes that line.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('No Practise line in x.7. ⚠ **The three moves are the examinable content and the third is the one that is skipped:** **say whether the question can be answered at all.** **And the mediator\'s limit must be said in the room:** **name the question and hand it to whoever can answer it** — **the mediator does not answer it, because the mediator does not know what the file is for either, and a comforting guess here produces exactly the harm of 15.7.**'));
