out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report – mediation (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['A page that does everything the unit has taught, and a candidate who cannot read it. Asked whether the page is wrong, Hiba said no — she wrote it and would write it again, and the candidate is right as well, which is the part she did not expect. So the mediation, which is three moves: separate what the page says from what the page is for; find the question the page does not answer; and say whether it can be answered at all. What it says is that three criteria were applied and one was failed, and that the overall verdict is a recommendation — every word accurate and the arithmetic published. The question it does not answer, Rim said, is what the fail means for her: whether it is a note for September, a condition on the recommendation, or something that will be read by somebody else in two years. Which is the finding of the cycle and it is new: a page can satisfy every criterion in this unit and still leave the person unable to act, because the five parts tell them how the verdict was reached and not what to do about it. Adnan said that is a real gap and he has it on every page he writes. The sentence that closes it is one line: the failed criterion is a note for your second year, it is not a condition and it does not go beyond this file — or the opposite, if the opposite is true. And Bassel asked what happens if the assessor does not know, and then that is the answer and it must be given: I do not know whether anybody else reads this file and I shall find out and tell you by Thursday. An assessor who does not know what their own page does is common, and the not-knowing is not the fault — leaving the candidate to guess is. Omar asked what the mediator actually does here when neither of them is wrong, and the mediator names the question and hands it to the person who can answer it, which is the whole job. The mediator does not answer it, because the mediator does not know what the file is for either, and a comforting guess here produces exactly the harm that 15.7 was about.']));
out.push(A('Listener task: the question the student\'s own last assessment does not answer, and who can answer it. ⚠ **Collect the second half, because it is where the cycle bites.** **In most rooms the person who can answer is not the assessor** — **it is whoever keeps the file** — **and almost nobody has asked them.** **That is the finding to leave on the board:** **the missing sentence is usually not hard to write; it is unwritten because nobody has asked the one question that would let them write it.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**✗** Redrafting the page. → **✓** the page is good; find the question.   **✗** _I am sure it is only a note._ → **✓** I do not know; I shall find out by Thursday.   **✗** Answering it as the mediator. → **✓** hand it to whoever can.   **✗** Treating Pair B as a missing question. → **✓** an unpublished criterion needs a reassessment.   **✗** _Both of you have a point._ → **✓** both accounts are accurate, and here is the question.'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read – exam practice (Reading and Use of English Part 4)'));
out.push(A('**1** _has ever been turned down_   **2** _prior to the reading of_   **3** _is no point in_ _(also accepted: **is no possibility of**)_   **4** _was not until_   **5** _No matter how_   **6** _has never made a difference_'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 2 is the one to mark hardest, because the word given forces a noun.** _Prior to_ **cannot take a clause**, so _prior to the papers were read_ is the commonest wrong answer and it is wrong on grammar rather than on meaning. **Item 3 needs a gerund after the preposition** — _no point in appealing_ — **and about a quarter of any room writes _no point to appeal_.** ⚠ **Item 5 is the only one where the given word starts the sentence**, and students who have learned to put the key word in the middle of the gap lose it on position alone. **Remind the room of the two rules that decide half the marks in this part:** **between two and five words including the word given, and the word given unchanged.**'));
