out.push(A('**206 words, inside the 180–220 band, no introduction, the verdict with its reader in the first line, the decisive detail carried by a figure _(eleven and four)_, the weakness given at full strength, and a repair the reader could act on.** ⚠ **The sentence that earns the band is _it is a complete account of how a verdict was reached, written for the file, and the file is not the person_** — **it is the whole cycle in one line and it concedes everything good about the instrument first.** **A review that calls the form vague has not read it and loses the content mark.**'));
out.push(S('Stage ✓ · Unit 16 check'));
out.push(A('**A** **1** b _(counts)_   **2** a _(which)_   **3** b _(against)_   **4** c _(appealable)_   **5** c _(objectivity)_   **6** b _(moderated)_   **7** a _(screened)_   **8** c _(consistency)_'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 1 catches more students than any other item in the unit**: **_the delivery record_ is the subject and not _the returns_**, so the verb is singular — **and a room that has spent six cycles saying _the returns count for half_ reaches for the plural.** **Read the subject aloud before the verb.** **Item 4 is the unit\'s word-formation hinge:** ⚠ **_appealed_ is what happened to a verdict and _appealable_ is what can be done to it**, and the sentence is about a property and not an event. **And item 6 is the past simple inside what looks like a vocabulary item** — **the moderation happened before the publishing, so both verbs are past.**'));
out.push(A('**B  Listening** **1** B   **2** A   **3** B   **4** B   **5** A   **6** B   **7** B'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 1\'s distractor A is the answer most rooms want** _(the form was too long)_ — **and she never says anything about length; she says nobody could say what one line meant.** **Item 3 needs the reason and not the authority:** **she publishes the weighting because effort goes to the wrong criterion otherwise, and she says so about her own year.** ⚠ **Item 7 is the one to replay.** **It is the last answer in the recording, it is the finding of the whole cycle, and the two distractors are things she demonstrably does have on her pages** — **which is the point: what is missing is not the working or the appeal route.** **Play the recording twice and give the room the standing instruction: read all seven stems before it starts.**'));
out.push(A('**C  Writing** — **marked on the four requirements of the task and nothing else:** **who it works for, who it does not, what decided the verdict, and what is wrong with it.** ⚠ **All four or the content mark goes**, and the commonest loss is the second: **a review that says who the instrument works for and never names who it fails has written a recommendation.** **The Stage 7 sample above is the band-5 model.**'));
